
# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:19
translate english scenario_2_96cd6425:

    # e "Sveicināts uz klāja!"
    e "Welcome aboard!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:23
translate english scenario_2_079fea34:

    # e "Kāpēc esam ārā? Iesim zvejot!"
    e "Why are we out here? Let's go fishing!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:27
translate english scenario_2_ff4c846f:

    # e "Tikai šoreiz Tu būsi loms, bet es - makšķernieks. Mans uzdevums būs Tevi pievilināt ar dažādām ēsmām."
    e "But this time, you'll be the catch - and I'll be the fisherman. My job will be to lure you in with all kinds of bait."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:28
translate english scenario_2_9e0da05a:

    # e "Bet kāpēc tādas lomas? Scenārijs būs par {u}pikšķerēšanu{/u}."
    e "But why those roles? This scenario will be about {u}phishing{/u}."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:29
translate english scenario_2_c51a06a3:

    # e "Tā ir kiberuzbrukumu metode, kas ar maldinošām metodēm mēģina pievilināt Tavu uzmanību un uzticību, lai iegūtu Tavus personīgos vai uzņēmuma datus."
    e "It's a type of cyberattack that uses deceptive tactics to grab your attention and gain your trust, in order to obtain your personal or company data."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:30
translate english scenario_2_8d529acb:

    # e "Angļu valodā šādus uzbrukumus sauc par {u}phishing attack{/u} - saskan ar vārdu \"fish\" - zivis!"
    e "In English, these attacks are called {u}phishing attacks{/u} - which sounds like the word \"fish\"!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:34
translate english scenario_2_5a5dd832:

    # e "Makšķeres galā ir ēsma - tā var būt aizdomīga e-pasta vēstule vai tīmekļa lapa, kas uz pirmā skatiena izskatās kā īsta."
    e "Bait is at the end of the line - it could be a suspicious email message or a website that looks real at first glance."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:35
translate english scenario_2_ef571b63:

    # e "Tavs uzdevums - spēt noteikt pazīmes, kas liecinātu par to, vai inforācija ir patiesa vai maldinoša."
    e "Your task is to identify the signs that indicate whether information is genuine or deceptive."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:37
translate english scenario_2_8309d4c2:

    # nvl_narrator "Jauns ziņojums"
    nvl_narrator "New message"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:38
translate english scenario_2_aa47a253:

    # p_nvl "Jums ir ienākuši 6 jauni e-pasti."
    p_nvl "You have 6 new emails."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:43
translate english scenario_2_3d1bc603:

    # e "Tieši laikā!"
    e "Right on time!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:47
translate english scenario_2_c5abcc34:

    # e "Krāpniekiem e-pasti ļooti patīk, jo ar tiem ikviens asprātis var izlikties par kādu uzticamu avotu. Turklāt e-pastus var izsūtīt plašam saņēmēju lokam vienlaicīgi, gaidot, kad kāds paķers ēsmu."
    e "Scammers loooove emails, because with them any clever trickster can pretend to be a trusted source. In addition, emails can be sent to a wide audience at once, hoping someone will take the bait."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:48
translate english scenario_2_3b8b544b:

    # e "Šķietami mazas nianses spēj palīdzēt pateikt priekšā, vai informācija patiesa. Arī zināšanas par metodēm, ar kādiem pikšķerētāji zvejo informāciju, ļoti noder. Bet vai Tu spēsi atšķirt īsto no neīstā?"
    e "Even seemingly minor details can tip you off to whether information is genuine. Knowing the methods phishers use to fish for information is also very useful. But can you tell the real from the fake?"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:49
translate english scenario_2_47dad172:

    # e "Pēc kārtas vērsi vaļā dažādus e-pastus, kas te sasūtīti. Kopumā būs 6 piemēri. Sākumā ēsmas centies noteikt ar savām acīm, tad veic izvēli, un pēc tam es visu paskaidrošu, ja kaut kas būs palaists garām."
    e "You'll open various emails one by one that have been sent here. There will be 6 examples in total. First, try to spot the bait with your own eyes, then make your choice, and afterwards I'll explain everything in case you missed anything."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:50
translate english scenario_2_9e46b413:

    # e "E-pastiem būs pogas un saites - uz tām klikšķināt nevar (uz nekādiem brīnumiem nevedīšu.. diemžēl {image=emoji/sweat.png}). Taču, turot kursoru virs tām, apakšā parādīsies saite, uz kurieni tās ved. Esi acīgs!"
    e "The emails will have buttons and links - you can't click them (I won't be taking you to any special surprises... unfortunately {image=emoji/sweat.png}). However, if you hover your cursor over them, the link's URL will appear at the bottom showing where it leads. Stay sharp!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:52
translate english scenario_2_7180a78c:

    # e "Lai nebūtu tik vienkārši, varbūt kāds e-pasts būs īsts. Kad tas apskatīts, spied jebkur uz ekrāna un veic izvēli par to, vai tas īsts vai ēsma!"
    e "To keep things from being too simple, maybe some of the emails will be real. Once you've looked at one, click anywhere on the screen and decide whether it's real or bait!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:55
translate english scenario_2_19df88f7:

    # e "Lai veicas!"
    e "Good luck!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:59
translate english scenario_2_33046f26:

    # "1. E-pasts - piedāvājums no \"{color=#FF0000}Coca-Cola{/color}\""
    "1. Email - offer from \"{color=#FF0000}Coca-Cola{/color}\""

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:68
translate english scenario_2_6a5b9637:

    # e "Nu, nu - esam uzmanīgāki."
    e "Now, now - let's be more careful."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:72
translate english scenario_2_76cfe930:

    # e "Pareizi! Piedāvājums tiešām pārāk labs, lai būtu īsts."
    e "Correct! The offer really was too good to be true."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:76
translate english scenario_2_0ba0580c:

    # e "Šis tik tiešām bija īsts mikslis!"
    e "This one was truly a mixed bag!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:80
translate english scenario_2_3a2b2fc2:

    # e "E-pasts apgalvo, ka ir no Coca-Cola, taču sūtītāja adrese ir ļoti nejauša - tas nav neiespējami arī īstam e-pastam, taču ir aizdomīgs signāls."
    e "The email claims to be from Coca-Cola, but the sender's address is very random-looking - not impossible for a real email, but still a red flag."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:81
translate english scenario_2_4512d4ec:

    # e "Saturs - pat teksts - viss ir ievietots vienā lielā attēlā. Lai gan dažos īstos e-pastos tas tiek izmantots, šī tehnika bieži tiek pielietota, lai izvairītos no atklāšanas."
    e "The content - even the text - is all embedded in one large image. While this is sometimes done in legitimate emails, attackers often use this technique to avoid detection."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:82
translate english scenario_2_8fba5446:

    # e "Saite neved uz Coca-Cola mājaslapu, un tā ir veidota tā, lai noslēptu pāradresācijas un novērstu lasītāja uzmanību - tā aktivizējas tikai ar tekstu pēc # zīmes. Vai spēji uzķert?"
    e "The link doesn't go to Coca-Cola's website, and it's crafted to hide redirects and distract the reader - it only activates using the text after the '#' symbol. Did you catch that?"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:85
translate english scenario_2_3fe6324d:

    # e "Kas tālāk?"
    e "What's next?"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:89
translate english scenario_2_13b76cba:

    # "2. E-pasts - ziņojums no Google"
    "2. Email - message from Google"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:98
translate english scenario_2_493f9754:

    # e "Pareizi! Šoreiz e-pasts pavisam īsts."
    e "Correct! This time the email is completely real."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:102
translate english scenario_2_ac0950a9:

    # e "Šoreiz nebūs pareizi. E-pasts ir pavisam reāls. Bet, kā saka - drošs paliek drošs. Nevaru dikti piesieties!"
    e "Not quite. This email is actually real. But, as they say - better safe than sorry. I can't really blame you for that!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:107
translate english scenario_2_344e5036:

    # e "Galvenā saite ir gara, kas var šķist aizdomīgi, bet šajā gadījumā tā ved uz oficiālu lietotāja konta lapu."
    e "The main link is long, which might seem suspicious, but in this case it leads to an official user account page."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:108
translate english scenario_2_fc0d4d2d:

    # e "Vērts zināt - īstie ziņojumi no Google vienmēr nāks no \"no-reply@accounts.google.com\" e-pasta. Sarakstu ar aktuālajiem brīdinājumiem var arī apskatīt apakšējā saitē."
    e "Good to know - genuine Google notifications will always come from the \"no-reply@accounts.google.com\" address. You can also view a list of current alerts at the link below."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:113
translate english scenario_2_37fc9461:

    # "3. E-pasts - dokuments no kolēģa"
    "3. Email - document from a colleague"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:122
translate english scenario_2_ce0890a3:

    # e "Nebūs pareizi - šis ir pikšķerētāja darbs."
    e "Not quite - this one is a phisher's work."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:126
translate english scenario_2_ab06f4ee:

    # e "Trāpīts! Būsi pamanījis maldinošo saiti."
    e "Spot on! You must have noticed the deceptive link."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:131
translate english scenario_2_2507f3a6:

    # e "Šis ir viens no visbīstamākajiem pikšķerēšanas veidiem. Redzi- te uzbrucējs tēlo kolēģi, iespējams pazīstamu, un ir izveidojis šķietami ticamu ziņojumu no Google Drive."
    e "This is one of the most dangerous types of phishing. You see - here the attacker is posing as a colleague, possibly someone you know, and has crafted a seemingly credible Google Drive message."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:132
translate english scenario_2_a68e6535:

    # e "Uzbrukumus, kas ir tieši mērķēti kādam darbiniekam vai uzņēmumam, sauc par aktīvi mērķētiem uzbrukumiem. Angliski tos sauc \"Spear phishing attack\" - tulkojas kā šķēpu zvejošana."
    e "Attacks aimed directly at a specific employee or company are called spear phishing attacks. Ouch!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:133
translate english scenario_2_4a2dd878:

    # e "Uzbrukumi var būt ļoti efektīvi, ja upuris vispirms rūpīgi nepārbauda informāciju. Šādi uzbrukumi ir retāki, jo uzbrucējam vispirms jāiegūst informācija par uzņēmumu vai personu."
    e "These attacks can be highly effective if the victim doesn't thoroughly verify the information first. Such attacks are less common, however, because the attacker has to gather information about the company or person beforehand."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:134
translate english scenario_2_66e4f384:

    # e "Kā varēja šo uzbrukumu atklāt? Pirmkārt, Google Drive ziņojumi nāks no pašas platformas e-pasta - ne no sūtītāja konta. Otrkārt, saitē svītras \"--\" imitē īsto saiti."
    e "How could this attack have been detected? First, Google Drive notifications come from the platform's own email address - not from the sender's account. Second, the double dashes \"--\" in the link were imitating the real URL."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:135
translate english scenario_2_ea87f4e1:

    # e "Tomēr - kas bija galvenais rādītājs? Saites sākumā redzamais HTTP protokols."
    e "However - what was the biggest giveaway? The presence of HTTP at the start of the URL."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:136
translate english scenario_2_b2fb8a34:

    # e "HTTP ir parasts interneta savienojums, bet HTTPS ir drošāks - tas šifrē informāciju, lai to nevarētu pārtvert vai nolasīt citi. Ja redzi \"https://\", tas nozīmē, ka vietne ir drošāka, taču ne vienmēr."
    e "HTTP is a standard internet connection, whereas HTTPS is more secure - it encrypts data so that others cannot intercept or read it. Seeing \"https://\" indicates the site is more secure, though that's not always the case."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:137
translate english scenario_2_67af79b4:

    # e "Ko vēl vērts zināt - tā kā lielākā daļa krāpnieku nezina tavu vārdu, viņi uzrunās tevi vispārīgos veidos ar standarta uzrunām."
    e "Another thing worth knowing - since most scammers don't know your name, they'll address you in generic ways with standard greetings."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:138
translate english scenario_2_5ccfb2be:

    # e "Ar darbu saistītos un personīgi adresētos e-pastos šim jāpievērš pastiprināta uzmanība, jo kolēģi parasti pazīst vai zin viens otru. Šajā gadījumā arī \"Laura\" uzrunā, neminot saņēmēja vārdu."
    e "For work-related or personally addressed emails, pay extra attention to this, because colleagues usually know each other by name. In this case, \"Laura\" greets the recipient without mentioning their name."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:142
translate english scenario_2_23efd58a:

    # e "Veram vaļā nākamo!"
    e "Let's open the next one!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:146
translate english scenario_2_202cfd2a:

    # "4. E-pasts - ziņa no Valsts ieņēmumu dienesta"
    "4. Email - message from the Latvian State Revenue Service"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:155
translate english scenario_2_356687f5:

    # e "Esi uzmanīgāks! Šī nav oficiāla VID saite."
    e "Be more careful! This is not an official Latvian State Revenue Service (VID) email."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:156
translate english scenario_2_d339cc83:

    # e "VID nekad ar Tevi tā nesazinātos."
    e "An official state institution would never contact you like that."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:160
translate english scenario_2_e5cdbfda:

    # e "Tieši tā! VID nekad ar Tevi tā nesazinātos."
    e "Exactly! An official Latvian state institution would never contact you like that."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:167
translate english scenario_2_c0834213:

    # e "Kas jāzin - VID un citas valsts institūcijas nesūta pieteikšanās saites e-pastā. Arī stils un valoda e-pastā nav formāla un stilistiski pareiza."
    e "Important to know - in Latvia VID and other government institutions don't send login links via email. Also, the style and language in the email are not formal or professionally written."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:168
translate english scenario_2_46ce7597:

    # e "Oficiālās VID lapas ir \"vid.gov.lv\" un \"eds.vid.gov.lv\". Arī varēja pamanīt, ka saite izmanto \"web.app\", kas bieži tiek izmantots pikšķerēšanai."
    e "The official State Revenue Service websites are \"vid.gov.lv\" and \"eds.vid.gov.lv\". You might also notice that the link uses \"web.app\", which is often used in phishing."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:169
translate english scenario_2_e6c715be:

    # e "Arī var manīt, ka e-pasta adrese \"@cuirsarie.fr\" nav saistīta ar VID. Valsts iestādes reti sūta e-pastus - labāka alternatīva ir E-adreses izmantošana, kas ir ļoti drošs variants."
    e "You can also tell that the sender's email address \"@cuirsarie.fr\" isn't associated with it. Government institutions rarely send emails - a better alternative they use is the official Latvian e-address system, which is a much more secure option."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:170
translate english scenario_2_e7b86148:

    # e "Pikšķerētāji ielikuši pieslēgšanās kodu, kas dod lasītājam maldīgu iespaidu par e-pasta autentiskumu. Ja tiek uzzvanīts, operatori var turpināt maldināt un pieprasīt sensitīvu informāciju."
    e "The phishers included a login code, which gives the reader a false impression of the email's authenticity. If you call it, the operators can continue to mislead you and request sensitive information."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:171
translate english scenario_2_d18c3b74:

    # e "Kopumā galvenais ieteikums - svarīgām saitēm pieslēgties tikai caur organizāciju oficiālajām saitēm no pārlūka."
    e "Overall, the main recommendation - for important accounts, only log in through the organization's official websites directly in your browser."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:175
translate english scenario_2_d5927d08:

    # e "Ejam tālāk!"
    e "Let's continue!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:179
translate english scenario_2_ad99b35a:

    # "5. E-pasts - ziņojums no \"{color=#0000FF}PayPal{/color}\""
    "5. Email - message from \"{color=#0000FF}PayPal{/color}\""

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:188
translate english scenario_2_b2588197:

    # e "Uzķēries! Esi uzmanīgāks."
    e "You took the bait! Be more careful."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:192
translate english scenario_2_c389adf9:

    # e "Tieši tā! Šis ir pikšķerētāja darbs."
    e "Exactly! This is a phisher's handiwork."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:196
translate english scenario_2_283f3d92:

    # e "Pikšķerēšanas e-pasti, kas tēlo finansiālus uzņēmumus, ir ļoti izplatīti, jo veiksmīgs uzbrukums var nest lielu peļņu."
    e "Phishing emails that impersonate financial companies are very common, since a successful attack can yield a large profit."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:201
translate english scenario_2_aa391504:

    # e "Šajā gadījumā varētu nodomāt, ka ar e-pastu viss ir kārtībā - tas ved uz droša tipa saiti, kā arī sūtītāja e-pasts var šķist ticams."
    e "In this case, one might think everything in the email looks okay - it leads to a secure-looking link, and the sender's email might appear credible."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:202
translate english scenario_2_73969b05:

    # e "Taču, pievēršot lielāku uzmanību, varēja manīt, ka saite patiesībā ved uz pavisam citu vietu - \"https://www.palpay.com\". Jau pēc nosaukuma redzams, ka kaut kas nav labi."
    e "However, if you paid closer attention, you could see that the link actually goes to a completely different site - \"https://www.palpay.com\". The name alone shows that something isn't right."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:203
translate english scenario_2_1edcdac5:

    # e "Tekstā izmantoti nezināmi un neizskaidroti iemesli problēmām. Raksturīga ir arī steidzība - viss jāizdara ātri un bez liekas domāšanas. Vizuālais izkārtojums arī varētu būt labāks."
    e "The email text gives vague, unexplained reasons for the problems. It also creates a sense of urgency - everything needs to be done quickly without much thought. The visual layout could have been better as well."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:204
translate english scenario_2_841b0307:

    # e "Pikšķerētājs maldina lasītāju, minot, ka paroles jāsargā un jāpiesakās tikai caur doto \"oficiālo\" saiti. Viss tā kā būtu pareizi, bet šādā veidā patscenšas izlikties par īsto un pareizo."
    e "The phisher misleads the reader by stating that passwords must be protected and that you should only log in through the provided \"official\" link. It all sounds correct, but in doing so he's trying to pose as the legitimate source."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:205
translate english scenario_2_069040e1:

    # e "Galvenā atziņa - pārbaudam gan e-pastā redzamo saiti, {u}gan{/u} tās reālo adresi ar kursoru."
    e "The main takeaway - always check both the link shown in the email {u}and{/u} its real URL by using your cursor."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:209
translate english scenario_2_6e2b75a5:

    # e "Pēdējais e-pasts - beidzot!"
    e "The last email - finally!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:213
translate english scenario_2_6d7af2aa:

    # "6. E-pasts - ziņa no \"{color=#0000FF}Dropbox{/color}\""
    "6. Email - message from \"{color=#0000FF}Dropbox{/color}\""

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:222
translate english scenario_2_0a2b4f23:

    # e "Trāpīts! Šis ir īsts ziņojums no Dropbox."
    e "Nailed it! This is a genuine notification from Dropbox."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:226
translate english scenario_2_49f90b85:

    # e "Šoreiz nebūs pareizi. Šis ir īsts ziņojums no Dropbox."
    e "Not quite. This is a legitimate Dropbox notification."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:231
translate english scenario_2_46c909cf:

    # e "Šeit ir redzams piemērs īstam un drošam e-pastam no uzticama sūtītāja."
    e "Here's an example of a legitimate, secure email from a trusted sender."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:232
translate english scenario_2_920142fa:

    # e "Lai arī pēc iepriekšējiem piemēriem saprotams, ka skatamies uz visu ar lielu skepsi, šoreiz, ja ieskatās, visas saites ir drošas un sūtītāja adrese nerada pamatu šaubām."
    e "After those earlier examples, it's understandable to look at everything with a lot of skepticism. But this time, if you look closely, all the links are secure and the sender's address doesn't raise any concerns."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:233
translate english scenario_2_f2690ad8:

    # e "Arī redzams, ka sūtītājs neprasa vai nepiedāvā paust savu personīgo informāciju - tā ir laba zīme."
    e "You can also see that the sender isn't asking for or prompting you to reveal any personal information - that's a good sign."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:237
translate english scenario_2_9adb449c:

    # e "Nu ko - būsim izskatījuši visu, kas bija sasūtīts. Cerams spēji atrast daļu makšķerētāju trikus!"
    e "Well, we've gone through everything that was sent. Hopefully you managed to spot some of the phishers' tricks!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:238
translate english scenario_2_3349b0a7:

    # e "Šeit vien bija pāris piemēri, bet patiesais daudzums ar veidiem, kādos pikšķerētāji apspēlē upurus, ir ievērojami lielāks."
    e "These were just a few examples, but the actual number of ways phishers try to trick victims is significantly larger."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:242
translate english scenario_2_6805cd5e:

    # e "Visu nekad nevar zināt, taču vienmēr ir vērts būt kritiskiem un ievērot drošas informācijas apmaiņas principus, lai uzbrucēji netiktu pie mūsu informācijas."
    e "You can never know everything, but it's always worth being critical and following safe information exchange practices so that attackers don't get hold of our information."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:246
translate english scenario_2_03dbe611:

    # e "Nobeigumā apskatīsim, kas notiktu, ja Tu tomēr uzspiestu uz kādu no neīstajām adresēm un nonāktu pikšķerētāja lapā."
    e "Finally, let's take a look at what would happen if you did click on one of the fake addresses and ended up on a phisher's page."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:247
translate english scenario_2_d2bc5f2a:

    # e "Izspēlēsim spēli, kurā Tu centīsies atrast {u}5{/u} pazīmes, kas liecina par pikšķerēšanas mēģinājumu."
    e "We'll play a game where you try to find {u}5{/u} signs that indicate a phishing attempt."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:248
translate english scenario_2_82e83849:

    # e "Priekšā būs bankas tīmekļa lapa. Spied uz tām vietām, kas Tev šķiet {u}aizdomīgas{/u}."
    e "Up next is a fake SEB bank's webpage. Click on the areas that seem {u}suspicious{/u} to you. If you want, you can open the official main website right now to see how it looks."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:249
translate english scenario_2_3750cb26:

    # e "Ja uzspiedīsi uz pareizās vietas, saņemsi punktu un zaļu zivtiņu. Ja uzspiedīsi uz nepareizās vietas, zaudēsi punktu un zivs būs sarkana. Tāpēc esi uzmanīgs!"
    e "If you click the right spot, you'll earn a point and a green fish will appear. If you click the wrong spot, you'll lose a point and the fish will be red. So be careful!"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:253
translate english scenario_2_7f9fba4b:

    # "Spēles uzdevums: tīmekļa lapā atrast 5 pazīmes, kas liecina par pikšķerēšanas mēģinājumu."
    "Game objective: find 5 signs on the webpage that indicate a phishing attempt."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:267
translate english phishing_end_4bb257b4:

    # e "Lieliski! Tu identificēji visas ēsmas, kas liecinātu, ka saite ir maldinoša."
    e "Great! You identified all the bait that would indicate the link was deceptive."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:271
translate english phishing_end_c2a975ee:

    # e "Nekad neievadi datus saitē, kamēr neesi pārliecinājies, ka tā ir droša."
    e "Never enter your data on a site until you are sure that it's secure."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:277
translate english phishing_end_bf7f6cbb:

    # nvl_narrator "Aizdomīgās pazīmes bija:"
    nvl_narrator "The suspicious signs were:"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:278
translate english phishing_end_04019ea0:

    # nvl_narrator "1. - logo, kas neatbilst SEB bankai"
    nvl_narrator "1. - a logo that doesn't match SEB Bank"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:279
translate english phishing_end_37fb4e89:

    # nvl_narrator "2. - drukas kļūda (Kodu klkulators)"
    nvl_narrator "2. - a typo (\"Code clculator\")"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:280
translate english phishing_end_b6a7297c:

    # nvl_narrator "3. - aizdomīgā pieslēgšanās poga (krāsa un fonts)"
    nvl_narrator "3. - the suspicious login button (color and font)"

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:281
translate english phishing_end_c7396c7f:

    # nvl_narrator "4. - \"https:bit.ly\" saite. Tādu uzbrucēji izmanto, ja vēlas paslēpt patieso adresi."
    nvl_narrator "4. - the \"https:bit.ly\" link. Attackers use those when they want to hide the real address."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:282
translate english phishing_end_ac9d974f:

    # nvl_narrator "5. - \"Not secure\" ziņa adreses joslā. Pārlūks brīdina, ja ir atvērta HTTP tipa saite. Arī zīme, ka lapa nav īsta."
    nvl_narrator "5. - the \"Not secure\" message in the address bar. The browser gives that warning when an HTTP site is open - another sign that the page isn't legit."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:290
translate english phishing_end_6cef9641:

    # e "Pēc visiem piemēriem var secināt, ka, lai neuzķertos uz krāpnieku āķiem, ir vienmēr jābūt kritiskiem un modriem, un secinājumus jāveido, izvērtējot vairākas pazīmes."
    e "From all these examples, we can conclude that to avoid getting caught on scammers' hooks, you must always remain critical and vigilant, and draw your conclusions by evaluating multiple signs."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:291
translate english phishing_end_c0f7313a:

    # e "Arī iesaku vienmēr nodalīt personīgos e-pastus no darba vai mācību vajadzībām paredzētiem. Kā arī jaunumiem, reklāmām un mazāk svarīgām vietnēm reģistrēties ar nodalītu e-pastu."
    e "I also recommend always keeping your personal email separate from the one you use for work or studies. Use a dedicated email address for newsletters, promotions, and other less important sites."

# game/scenarios/scenario_2.rpy:292
translate english phishing_end_de107958:

    # e "Tādā veidā var samazināt \"spam\" jeb mēstuļu skaitu svarīgos e-pastos."
    e "That way you can reduce the amount of \"spam\" (junk mail) in your important inboxes."

